president Donald Trump is so confident  in the drug he himself dubbed a  game-changer against kovat 19 that he  himself takes one pill of  hydroxychloroquine with zinc every  morning yeah I've taken it for about a  week and a half now and I'm still here  the president's unsolicited admission  came at the end of a winding press  conference next to restaurant executives  about reopening the country what do you  have to lose okay what do you have to  lose that's despite no evidence of the  drug working to prevent infection and  Trump's own Food and Drug Administration  warning against fusing  hydroxychloroquine to treat kovat  outside of an emergency hospital setting  a leading government immunologist  testified before congress last week that  he was demoted after doubting  hydroxychloroquine efficacy we also knew  that there were potential safety risk  for chloroquine to cause irregular  irregular heart rhythms and even in some  cases death a greater portion of US  military veterans who took the drug to  treat kovat 19 did die according to a  government study as compared to fellow  kovat patients who did not take  hydroxychloroquine and to larger studies  from New York found the drug offered no  significant benefit to hospitalized  patients Trump said his faith in  hydroxychloroquine comes from anecdotes  that make their way to the Oval Office  here's my evidence I get a lot of  positive calls about it  the American Medical Association says it  strongly opposes the non-fda-approved  use of hydroxychloroquine without  careful consultation with one's doctor  Trump says he has the White House  doctors approval he says he asked for it  himself  Heidi Joe Castro al Jazeera Washington
 

